// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Root cause of attempt 33's 4.1% accuracy:
// The model generates the correct multi-term expression in free text (e.g.,
// "n1 + n1 * mult + n2 + n3") but then opens a constrained span and immediately
// generates only one identifier, yielding "<<n1>>".  This happens because the
// arithmetic expression parser accepts a single identifier as a *complete*
// prefix, so CloseSpanIfComplete fires after the very first token.
//
// Primary fix: After entering constrained mode, run PenalizedConstrainedStep
// with eosToken penalized by 15.0 for the first 10 constrained steps.  This
// makes EOS far less likely than any binary operator, so the model continues
// generating past the first identifier and produces a multi-term expression
// that matches its own free-text reasoning.
//
// Secondary fix: Updated guidance (no <<>>) tells the model that EXPR must
// combine ALL relevant variables, not just one. This primes the model to
// write the full formula in its free-text chain-of-thought, which the EOS-
// penalized constrained generator then faithfully replicates inside the span.
