//     postconditions with ConstrainedStep – the returned token is either eosToken
//     (we break, state unchanged) or a hard-masked parser-valid token.
//     AppendConstrainedToken's postcondition gives IsValidPrefix of the extended
//     prefix. ✓
//
//   Phase 3 (CloseSpanIfComplete + ConstrainedStep loop): CloseSpanIfComplete
//     either closes (insideConstrainedOut := false, implication vacuously true,
//     currentConstrainedOut := []) or is a no-op (state unchanged). The
//     ConstrainedStep path preserves validity via AppendConstrainedToken. ✓
//
//   Phases 4/8/9-close (CloseSpanWithinBudget): library postcondition guarantees
//     insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut). ✓
//
